# Common Rules

Framework-agnostic style + naming. Placement/layering: see `layering.mdc` and `decisions.mdc`.

## Naming

| Type | File | Notes |
|------|------|-------|
| Nest controller / service / module | `auth.controller.ts`, `auth.service.ts`, `auth.module.ts` | Nest convention under `apps/api` |
| Web feature / component | `sign-in-form.tsx` | kebab-case files; PascalCase component exports |
| Route entry (Next) | `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx` | framework-required names |
| shadcn UI | under `apps/web/components/ui/` | |

- Classes / interfaces / types: `PascalCase`
- Functions / vars: `camelCase`
- Constants: `as const` objects, not TypeScript `enum`
- Directories: `kebab-case`, named by **domain/concern** (see `decisions.mdc`)

## Style

- **Prettier** (root `prettier.config.js`) is the format authority: 2 spaces, single quotes, no semicolons, printWidth ~100, no trailing commas
- Prefer `import type`; avoid `any`; prefer `| null` over `undefined` for optionals
- Run `pnpm format` / `pnpm format:check`; do not fight Prettier with one-off style

## Security baseline (always)

| Rule | Notes |
| ---- | ----- |
| No hardcoded secrets | env / secret manager only |
| No server secrets in client bundles | tokens in `localStorage` are session material — still never commit secrets |
| Validate external input at boundaries | Zod (or equivalent) at API/form edges |
| Parameterized DB access only | Drizzle / query builder — no string-built SQL |
| No production stack traces to clients | map via error filters/handlers |

## Quality

Smallest relevant set before claiming done (see also `invariants.mdc` DoD):

```bash
pnpm run lint
pnpm run format:check
pnpm run typecheck
pnpm run test
```
